ly endless stream of guinea pigs  like to feed to Halloween every night so  that Halloween doesn't go on a rampage  he's also as The Story Goes On like  becoming more and more convinced that  Halloween is taunting him specifically  for reasons that he can't really begin  to Fathom the day of the Fall Festival  is fast approaching though and Barry is  kind of dreading through like going  through this whole ordeal again  everybody does because they know that at  least one person is going to get the dot  but you know it's it's just kind of  leading up to that this year though a  few things turn out differently than  usual  for one thing and I'm not going to spoil  all the things that happen but for one  thing the Town Council decides to bring  in an outside company to set up some  rides at the festival like they never  had rides at the festival before  um and obviously nobody in town knows  how to like set up carnival rides so  they had to like bring in an outside uh  you know an outside company to do it and  that means that there's going to be a  handful of strangers in the town for the  first time in ages and ages now  everybody in town kind of knows the  rules no one is supposed to tell  Outsiders about what's going on in the  town like even if they talk to their  friends or relatives like outside of the  town like on the phone or whatever like  you're that's just kind of like an  understood thing that no one's supposed  to tell anybody about Halloween or what  goes on there but uh in this case things  end up getting a little more complicated  when Barry is cajoled for various  reasons into housing two of the carnies  uh that come there to set up the rides  and that's kind of like the inciting  incident that you know leads to the  conclusion leads to the climax so I mean  this was just a very very short suitably  spooky but like I said more on the Grim  depressing end not like the fun ookie  spooky end  um but it is like very entertaining  slice of Halloween goodness you know  what I mean if you want something to get  in the mood because it's so brief uh  there isn't a hell of a lot of character  development especially of kind of like a  lot of the peripheral characters and  there also isn't much backstory given to  um the history of the town or why  Halloween stalks this place specifically  uh most of the story is actually kind of  like the setup like explaining like the  deal and everything I mean you are  seeing things through Barry's character  like through the whole time but a lot of  it is just kind of like explaining you  know what's going on like why things are  the way they are  um so it actually in that way it kind of  reads a little bit more like a fable  and like not too much I don't want to go  too far in that direction but it is very  a little bit fable-like and it actually  does seem to be satirizing at least to a  degree and I could just be totally  reading this into it um so you know  forgive me but it seems that it's kind  of satirizing the extent to which  people can eventually become like  compliant and maybe like apathetic  towards any circumstance even like a  really horrific one like the one that  these townspeople are experiencing now  as I mentioned the main character Barry  isn't terribly sympathetic because he's  just very brooding and resigned but  that's kind of like the point of the  story though like I said I think that's  at least kind of how I read it and he  does get a little bit more proactive  like as The Story Goes On so you do kind  of start to root for them as [ __ ] starts  to get worse and worse  um now I will say just as a little  nitpick there are there were some like  grammatical errors in there like a  couple instances with differences  between their th uh eir like being  confused with t-h-e-y apostrophe Ari  like not not many I've played like I've  read some that were like way worse than  that but this could have gone like a  little bit more like fine-tooth comb in  with like a with an editor because there  were like a few grammatical errors but  not so many that it really like  distracted me all that much but I did  notice it so I will point it out  um but overall I'm gonna say like if  you're you're looking for just like very  succinct little shot in the arm of  Halloween fun uh typical like I said  it's not super fun but like just  Halloween story uh to put you in the  mood for the season then uh you know  this one is absolutely worth reading and  I actually really enjoyed it quite a bit  so that'll do it for this tomes of  Terror I will see you guys again for  another Halloween book on the next one  bye


